cff-version: 1.2.0
title: BERIL Knowledge Wiki
message: >-
  Compiled by software from AI-conducted research reports and not peer-reviewed.
  Cite the specific page and access date; for a finding, prefer the underlying
  research report linked from its summary page.
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A compiled, hub-structured scientific wiki over the BERIL Research
  Observatory's corpus of AI-conducted microbial-biology research reports:
  topic hubs with PubMed-verified literature context, cross-project concept
  syntheses, per-claim citations, recorded conflicts, and negative results.
authors:
  - name: The BERIL Project
    address: Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory
    city: Berkeley
    region: California
    country: US
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
license-url: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html
repository-code: https://github.com/beril-doe/beril-wiki
url: https://beril-doe.github.io/beril-wiki
keywords:
  - microbial genomics
  - pangenomics
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - bacterial fitness
  - knowledge base
